  "result": "Fixed: the quote now prints **27.06** (it was printing 26.09).\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/money.py`, `to_cents` padded the decimal part with a zero on the wrong side. `frac.rjust(2, \"0\")` turned `\"12.5\"` into `\"05\"`, so the price became 1205 cents instead of 1250. Two of those plus 8.25% tax gives 26.09. I changed it to `frac.ljust(2, \"0\")`, so `\"5\"` becomes `\"50\"`. Prices with two decimals or none convert the same as before.\n\n**Tests:** pytest isn't installed, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`, and all 6 pass. None of them caught this bug, though. A test that `to_cents(\"12.5\") == 1250` would cover it; I haven't added one.",
